    "pressure": {
      "file": "torsional_coupling_pressure.glb",
      "title": "Soft in torsion: detunes and damps vibration",
      "description": "A reciprocating engine delivers torque in pulses (here 6 per revolution). The soft rubber element lets the flywheel and the driven hub twist relative to each other, so the large flywheel oscillation (yellow mark) is strongly reduced at the hub. Choosing the torsional stiffness moves the system's torsional natural frequencies away from the engine firing orders (a torsional vibration analysis, TVA), and rubber hysteresis damps what remains; the damping heat must stay within the element's allowable power loss.",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
